WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:03.336
[music playing]

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:08.274
Oh, dammit, slipped chain.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.576
[exhales] I hate these.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:12.612
Small limbs like that, it
happens with chain saws.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:15.715
I got to fix this up.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:18.752
The fun ain't over yet.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:21.054
[engine revving]

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:25.058
OK.

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:27.060
I got my poles.

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:30.230
Time to get to work.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.065
What I want to do is
get this bark off.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:36.636
Then I'm going to make a point
and drive it in the ground.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.471
One of the benefits of
living in the woods,

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:41.474
you got to be creative.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.977
If you're not creative,
you're going to struggle.

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:46.112
[banging]

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:48.181
Try to use a little bit
of caveman knowledge

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.483
to make things a little
more comfortable.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:56.956
I'm able to survive out here.

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.792
But I want to thrive
out here, too.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:02.095
OK.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.630
Bench is done.

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.765
Woo, hoo, hoo!

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.667
You guys want to check it
out and have some hot choc?

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:08.435
KIDS: Yeah.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:13.006
SON: That's cooler
than I expected.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:14.073
RICK DEWILDE: It's awesome, huh?

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.276
SON: Yeah.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.777
We got our rocks.

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:18.978
We got our cottonwood.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:21.548
We got our bench, nice backrest.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:22.816
You see how this thing is?

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:23.750
Look.

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:26.219
See how it just smolders?

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:30.089
Before Western society came,
before there was matches,

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:33.793
and lighters, and stuff, this
is how back in the day people

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.195
carried their spark.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.930
Because believe me,
no matter how good

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.965
you are at making a
fire, you wouldn't be

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.967
able to make one at 50 below.

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:43.036
And without this spark,
without this birch punk

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:45.872
right here, easily we
could not be here today.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:49.476
We'd be wiped out, extinct
in this area of the Earth.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.377
Whatever created us
and created the earth

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.646
made it possible with
tools like this growing

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:56.282
right on the trees.

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:59.752
So that's good to
think about, you know.

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:01.254
I know what was my
favorite part of the day.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.055
What?

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:03.423
This.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.891
This is your favorite part.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.659
Good one.

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:07.727
Now that these gnats are
gone, we got the perfect spot.

